  "schema": "elder-souls/npcs@1",
  "group": "quest-givers",
  "owner": "W1-07 round 4 — race and standing on the quest-offer path",
  "source": "Every `giver.npc_id` under game/data/quests/** that had NO record anywhere in game/data/npcs/**. Nineteen people, nine of them carrying a `disposition_min`. `gate.js canOffer()` reads `num(undefined) === 0`, so each of those nine was a hard, race-invariant, UNPASSABLE gate that reported itself as an ordinary standing shortfall — the round-2 tool critic measured nine identical `disposition 0/N` clauses across six character signatures. The other ten give no disposition_min and were still invisible to RI-CHR02 method 4.",
  "consumed_by": "Engine.seedDispositions() writes `disposition` into sim.quest.dispositions; Engine._questDispositionModel() reads `reaction_group`, `race` and `faction` to derive what the person actually feels; gate.js canOffer() checks the result against giver.disposition_min. Engine._assertGiversAreVisibleToRace() refuses to boot if any giver in the book is missing from here.",
  "hand_authored": true,
  "generated_by": null,
  "do_not_regenerate": "Hand-authored. Every greeting, topic pair, reaction group and base disposition was chosen against a named quest and a named place. A generator that rewrites this file will silently re-open the defect it closed.",
  "reaction_group_note": "Chosen from the person and the place, not from convenience. speaker-teel-ashaan is RG-DEEP at disposition 50 because RI-MTH06 §A's worked example is stated against exactly that record: a dunmer/lukiul reaches a ceiling of 34 against Q-DEEP-01's ask of 50 and is refused for good, while a dunmer/interior reaches 60 and is not.",
  "topic_note": "Each record's topics are (actor, topic) pairs the shipped topic corpus can answer for all ten races, and at least one of each pair answers a different race differently — so these people are neither mute nor decorative under tools/analysis/creation-audit.mjs's dialogue section.",
  "declared_incomplete": {
    "owner": "W1-04 (settlement population) and W1-17 (dialogue volume)",
    "missing": [
      "schedules",
      "the rest of each settlement around these people",
      "quest-specific topic bodies"
    ]
  },
